hi this is kevin van ORD standing in for  reviewer Daniel Starkey to tell you  about super smash brothers yes there's  so much raw joy to be found in Super  Smash Brothers for the 3ds the game's  new emphasis on competitive modes will  be Kindle that competitive spirit within  you the trophies for characters like  pac-man and Megaman will unearth trivia  for games that may have been before your  time and the excellent soundtrack will  fuel your nostalgia for games like Zelda  and Pokemon  unlike most fighting games there are no  life bars and extensive button  combinations to learn in Super Smash  Brothers each characters attacks are  easy to learn and the goal is to rack up  damage to knock your opponent further  and further away eventually you'll be  able to knock your folk clear off the  stage it's like a trumped up glitzy  version of sumo wrestling and it's  brilliant if you're skilled or lucky  enough you can stay on a stage even  after taking more than your fair share  of hits this adds a layer of tension to  most matches as dealing the most damage  doesn't always guarantee your win the  3ds game lacks some widely panned  mechanics from the last game in the  series Super Smash Brothers Brawl gone  is the random tripping as well as the  general feeling of the low gravity  floatiness in their stead are a bevy of  subtle new additions aimed at both  casual players and the core crowd the  result feels more honest and broadly  appealing than  consideration  there are numerous features introduced  in Smash Brothers 3ds mid-battle items  are weirder and have a wider variety  effects including quite a few that can  deliver one bit Kos and another that  will give you an extra life levels and  fighters also have new additions to help  keep fights meaning fresher this time  around at higher levels of play  Nintendo's made tweaks to almost every  area from grabs to ledge guarding even  classic Smash Brothers concepts like  directional influence have been  overhauled the main cast of characters  has balloons 249 which is a far cry from  the 12 found in the original Nintendo 64  release almost all of the characters  played differently stages are similarly  varied and have a wide variety of  hazards and tricks to keep players  engaged at monster  they smash mothers stages have always  been incredibly diverse and it's great  to see that the imaginative levels  haven't been lost in the transition from  living room consoles to handheld it may  however cause some problems for your  hands and wrists playing on a small  handheld system is vastly different to  play on console controllers which are  engineered to be extremely comfortable  to use for hours on end it's worth  mentioning that if you're going to be  picking this game up you might want to  try the demo of it if you're using one  of the smaller 3ds models to make sure  your hands don't cramp up  Smash Brothers 3ds has two online modes  to choose from for fun and for glory the  former has the full standard list of  stages available and signature Smash  Brothers items like the beam sword and  homerun bat will appear regularly in the  latter every stages of variants of the  final destination location meaning it's  completely flat and has no special  characteristics items are banned from  these matches in an effort to more  closely mimic at the kind of a  competitive environment that has grown  up around the series single-player modes  are pretty minimal on the 3ds especially  compared to Super Smash Brothers Brawl  but what's here is fantastic classic  mode is back and while the 3ds version  might seem a little bit shorter than in  previous games it's also by far the best  before each run you'll wager gold coins  that you've earned by playing matches  the more you wager the tougher the  fights but that also ups the rewards and  collectables you can earn at the end  you'll collect your winnings possibly  unlock a new character and do something  else or play through again which is what  you'll probably do a lot  you can spend the gold you pick up in an  in-game store to unlock through trophies  or you can play other modes like trophy  rush which costs a certain amount of  gold per second of play in all of these  modes the goal is to unlock more of  Smash Brothers many many many secrets  hidden stages characters items to  upgrade your Me's and trophies all pull  from the Nintendo Pantheon and are all  meant to be something special to some  fans somewhere what matters most is that  Super Smash Brothers 3ds just feels  great to play Smash Brothers it's good  to have you back
 

